    "narrative": "For the June 22nd slate, **Corbin Carroll** (76.69) and **Brice Turang** (73.68) headline our production expectations. **Corbin Carroll** remains our cornerstone, benefiting from an advantageous matchup against Pallante and, crucially, a slow pitcher delivery profile that maximizes his elite stolen base upside. Similarly, **Brice Turang** sees his stock rise significantly behind an 11% boost from the SP skill profile and favorable wind conditions that push his projection into the strong tier. Meanwhile, **Jose Caballero** (69.99) is our most aggressive platoon play; his 13% boost against a left-handed starter, paired with the high-likelihood of a stolen base against the vulnerable Valdez, makes him an essential piece of this lineup despite his lower batting order position.\n\nWe are navigating a few high-risk profiles today, primarily with **James Wood** (51.16) and **Austin Riley** (57.02). **James Wood** faces a sharp efficiency headwind due to a high-caliber opposing catcher; despite his elite xwOBA, his score is tempered by the risk of limited baserunning opportunities. **Austin Riley** narrowly missed a promotion to the active starting nine, sitting just behind the higher-upside efficiency of our bottom-order speed threats. While our bench is currently hampered by the absences of **Mickey Moniak**, **Trevor Story**, and **Giancarlo Stanton** due to IL designations\u2014and with **Josh Naylor** off the slate entirely\u2014we remain confident in the current configuration. We are monitoring the pending lineup statuses for **Dalton Rushing**, **Alex Freeland**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Kyle Karros**, and **Austin Riley**; should any of these players be moved into unfavorable spots, we are prepared to pivot to keep our team-wide efficiency at the highest possible threshold.",
